</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs7">
<td width="17.029%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Rotate Viewport</span></p>
</td>
<td width="73.596%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table">Using this command an object can be rotated by an exact entry of degree around a specified axes.</p>
</td>
<td width="9.375%" class="whs30">
<p class="normal-table" style="text-align:center;" align="center"><a href="../References/Rotate_Viewport.htm" target="_self"><img src="Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs31" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs7">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="17.029%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Create Viewport Entity</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="73.596%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table">This command creates an entity that stores the current viewport orientation. This entity can be selected at any time to restore the view.</p>
<p class="normal-table">This entity is located in <u style="font-weight:bold; text-decoration:none;"><span style="font-weight:bold; text-decoration:none;"><b>View Position</b></span></u> group. It is not graphically represented in the scene; its appearance is in the <u><a href="Entities_Pane.htm" target="_self">Entities pane</a></u> only. Viewport entity can be reselected at any time to restore the view - right click on the viewport name and select Use from the <u><a href="Tree_Context_Menus.htm#Specific_commands_for_View_Positions" target="_self">tree context menu</a></u>. If you select Set to Current View, you will change the viewport orientation to the current one.</p>
<p class="normal-table"><img src="Images/custom_views.jpg" width="245px" height="236px" border="0" class="img_whs39" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="9.375%" class="whs30">
<p class="normal-table" style="text-align:center;" align="center"><a href="../References/Create_Viewport_Entity.htm" target="_self"><img src="Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs31" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs7">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="17.029%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table-func">Align to Plane</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="73.596%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">Aligns view direction orthogonal to the selected datum plane or plane reducible datum entity (cylinder, circle, cone, slots).</span> This command is N/A in <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Inspection mode</i></span>.</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="9.375%" class="whs30">
<p class="normal-table" style="text-align:center;" align="center"><a href="../References/align_to_plane.htm" target="_self"><img src="Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs31" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
