<p class="caption">Command</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="73.596%" class="whs26">
<p class="caption">Description</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="9.375%" class="whs27">
<p class="caption">Details</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs7">
<td width="17.029%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Adjust</span></p>
</td>
<td width="73.596%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table">Adjusts the light direction in the scene. The mouse pointer changes to bulb<img src="Visualisation_menu_files/image004.gif" width="33px" height="35px" border="0" class="img_whs42" alt="">. While holding the left mouse button, drag the mouse pointer to a desired position. Light changing is valid for the active window only. Direction of the light is stored so next time when you run KUBE , the new lighting will be used for the scenes of all open documents.</p>
</td>
<td width="9.375%" class="whs30">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/Light_Adjust.htm" target="_self"><img src="Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs31" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs7">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="17.029%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Reset</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="73.596%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table">Resets the light direction to its original orientation.</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="9.375%" class="whs30">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/Light_Reset.htm" target="_self"><img src="Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs31" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p><span lang="EN-US"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Use in</b>:</span> Adjusting light is useful when some areas of an object are shaded and you want to see the details.<span lang="EN-US">&#160;</span></p>
<p class="sub-head"><span style="text-decoration:underline;"><u><a name="Play"></a></u></span>Play</p>
<p>Displays an animated rotated view of the visible entities in the current document. During rotation scan data are displayed as points, meshes as polygons, all other types as their current state. This mode acts as a screensaver press a button on the keyboard or move the mouse to exit. This command is N/A in <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Inspection mode</i></span>.<span lang="EN-US">&#160;</span><a href="../References/Play.htm" target="_self"><img src="Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs31" alt=""></a></p>
