<td width="73.596%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table">Shows/hides the grid.</p>
</td>
<td width="9.375%" class="whs30">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/display_grid.htm" target="_self"><img src="Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs31" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs45">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="17.029%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Display Normals</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="73.596%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table">Shows/hides point normals as short yellow lines. This command is applicable to scan data and meshes only. The state of <span class="Command">Display Normals</span> is not stored so next time when you run KUBE , the command will be disabled. This command is N/A in <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Inspection mode</i></span>.</p>
<p class="normal-table"><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Use in</b>:</span></b> <span class="Command">Display Normals</span> is useful when importing 3D data in other formats. Sometimes orientation of the normals in KUBE does not correspond to other CAD applications. It is better to see which areas are faulty before unifying normals.</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="9.375%" class="whs30">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/display_normals.htm" target="_self"><img src="Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs31" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
